-- Companion to aggregate_taking_container.
--
-- An aggregate over a container may pick up the attribute from one of the
-- classes that might be contained, even when the class guaranteed for all of
-- them does not have it, because the generated code only aggregates over
-- instances of the class defining the attribute.
--
-- That only works as long as ONE single content class defines it. Here both
-- 'garment' and 'gadget' define their own 'cover', and they are unrelated, so
-- there is no class to select the instances to aggregate over and this must
-- still be reported as error 316.

The room Isa location
End the.

The hero Isa actor At room
  Is total 0.
End the.

The closet Isa entity
  Container Taking garment.
End the.

Every garment Isa thing
  Is cover 0.
  Container Taking gadget.
End every.

Every gadget Isa thing
  Is cover 0.
End every.

Verb probe
  Does
    Set total Of hero To Sum Of cover In closet.
End verb.

Start At room.
